  "description": "This dataset comprises 169 resting-state electroencephalograms (EEGs) from COVID-19 survivors (n=86) and close contacts/healthy controls (n=83), acquired using standard 10-20 electrode montage. The study investigates neurophysiological signatures of COVID-19 infection through quantitative EEG analysis, comparing spectral and functional connectivity patterns between groups and against a Cuban normative database. The dataset includes 8 minutes of eyes-closed resting EEG, followed by alternating eye-state conditions, providing a comprehensive neurophysiological characterization of post-COVID neurological sequelae.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded using a 10-20 standard montage. Resting-state EEG was acquired for 8 minutes with eyes closed in all participants, followed by 2 minutes of alternating closed and open eyes, and 2 minutes of recovery.",
